# Subscription Blueprints

## Architecture: Push model (not Pull)

Recurio Blueprints **stamp settings directly onto products** via `stamp_settings_on_product()`.
Products hold a back-reference `_recurio_blueprint_id` post meta.
This differs from pull-model competitors: no runtime plan lookup happens on the product page.

## Key invariants to preserve

- **`slug` is unique** — always generated via `unique_slug()` on create/duplicate; never user-supplied.
- **`status` lifecycle:** `draft` → `active` (auto on first `apply`) → `archived` (soft delete; DELETE endpoint).
  Never hard-delete a blueprint row — subscriptions use linked product meta, not the blueprint row directly.
- **Propagation flag:** `PUT /blueprints/{id}?propagate=true` triggers `propagate_to_linked_products()`
  which iterates `_recurio_blueprint_id` post meta holders and calls `stamp_settings_on_product()` on each.
  This must always re-apply the current `settings` JSON, not a diff.
- **Analytics** are computed on-the-fly from `recurio_subscriptions` and `recurio_subscription_revenue`.
  No separate analytics cache table. Keep `get_analytics()` query efficient (uses `IN (product_ids)`).

## Settings fields — keep in sync in three places

Any new billing setting must be added to **all three**:
1. `sanitize_settings()` whitelist in `class-blueprints-api.php`
2. `stamp_settings_on_product()` `$meta_map` in `class-blueprints-api.php`
3. Step 2 of `BlueprintWizard.vue`

Current fields: `billing_period`, `billing_interval`, `trial_days`, `signup_fee`,
`signup_fee_type`, `discount_type`, `discount_value`, `payment_type`, `max_payments`,
`subscription_length`, `allow_one_time_purchase`.

`allow_one_time_purchase` is stored as `'yes'`/`'no'` inside the settings JSON (matches
`_recurio_allow_one_time_purchase` product meta convention). The Vue checkbox sends a
boolean; `sanitize_settings()` converts it to `'yes'`/`'no'`. `enrich_row()` returns the
raw string, so the wizard `watch` coerces it back to boolean before binding.

## Blueprint types

`subscribe_save` | `recurring` | `installment`

Changing the enum → update `$allowed_types` array in `extract_blueprint_data()` AND the
`types` array in `BlueprintWizard.vue` (both `value` and `desc`).

## DB schema

Table: `{prefix}recurio_blueprints` — `id`, `name`, `description`, `slug`, `type`, `status`,
`settings` (LONGTEXT JSON), `created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`.
Created in `create_database_tables()` (new installs) and `upgrade_to_1_0_4_blueprints()` (existing).
DB version gate: `recurio_db_version < 1.0.4` in `maybe_upgrade_database()` — `recurio.php`.

## REST endpoints (`recurio/v1/blueprints`)

All require `manage_woocommerce` capability via `check_permission()`.

| Method | Path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/blueprints` | `page`, `per_page`, `search`, `type`, `status` params |
| POST | `/blueprints` | `name` required |
| GET/PUT/DELETE | `/blueprints/{id}` | PUT accepts `propagate` bool param |
| POST | `/blueprints/{id}/apply` | `product_ids[]` required; auto-promotes to `active` |
| GET/DELETE | `/blueprints/{id}/products` | DELETE needs `product_id` param |
| GET | `/blueprints/{id}/analytics` | Live query — no caching |
| POST | `/blueprints/{id}/duplicate` | Creates `{name} (Copy)` as `draft` |

## Vue layer

- **`Blueprints.vue`** — list page; summary tiles; filter bar (search + type + status); El-Table
  with row-click → detail drawer; archive uses `ElMessageBox.confirm`.
- **`BlueprintWizard.vue`** — dialog with `el-steps`; step 0 = name/type cards; step 1 = billing;
  step 2 = `BlueprintProductPicker` (create mode only). Edit mode skips step 2, shows propagation toggle.
- **`BlueprintAnalyticsCard.vue`** — fetches `/blueprints/{id}/analytics`; metric grid.
- **`BlueprintProductPicker.vue`** — remote-search uses `/products` endpoint; apply calls
  `/blueprints/{id}/apply`; detach calls DELETE `/blueprints/{id}/products`.

API calls use the shared axios instance from `@/services/api`.

## Category / Tag Scope

Blueprints carry `scope_category_ids` and `scope_tag_ids` inside the `settings` JSON (sanitised
as integer arrays in `sanitize_settings()`). These drive two things:

### Priority system (`_recurio_blueprint_link_type` post meta)

| Value | Priority | Set by |
|---|---|---|
| `direct` | 3 (highest) | Merchant applies manually |
| `tag` | 2 | `apply-scope` matched a tag |
| `category` | 1 (lowest) | `apply-scope` matched a category |

`can_stamp($product_id, $incoming_link_type)` checks the existing link type and returns `false`
if a higher-priority link already exists. Never call `stamp_settings_on_product()` without
checking `can_stamp()` first (except for `direct` links, which always win).

### Auto-enroll new products

`maybe_auto_stamp_product()` runs on `save_post_product`. It fetches all active blueprints with
a scope, compares their category/tag IDs against the product's terms, and stamps the best match.
Skips products already carrying a `direct` link type.

### New REST endpoints

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/blueprints/{id}/apply-scope` | Apply to all products matching scope; respects priority |
| GET | `/blueprints/{id}/scope-coverage` | Dry-run count + term labels |
| GET | `/blueprints/taxonomy-search` | Term search for `product_cat` / `product_tag` |

### Vue scope tab (wizard step 3)

Two tabs: "By Product" (`BlueprintProductPicker`) and "By Category / Tag" (remote `el-select`
for categories + tags, coverage preview button, "Apply scope now" button).

### `BlueprintProductPicker.vue`

Shows Direct / Tag / Category badge on each row. Only `direct`-linked products have an active
Remove button. Scope-linked products show a tooltip: "Remove via category/tag scope to detach."

## Product edit page

`class-woocommerce-product.php` renders an "Active Blueprint" notice in the Subscription tab
when `_recurio_blueprint_id` is set. Displays both the blueprint name and the link type label
("Direct link", "via Tag", "via Category") with a contextual tooltip. `save_blueprint_meta()`
persists the ID on WC save; `_recurio_blueprint_link_type` is managed by the REST API only
(not overwritten on product save unless the blueprint_id is cleared).
